<title>USA: BT consortium wins UK defense contract.</title>
<headline>BT consortium wins UK defense contract.</headline>
<dateline>GAITHERSBURG, Md. 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>A consortium led by British Telecommunications has won a $1.55 billion, 10-year contract to provide a national fixed telecommunications network for the British armed forces, Lockheed Martin Corp said Friday.</p>
<p>The consortium includes Lockheed, GEC Marconi Secure Systems and GPT Strategic Communications Systems.  </p>
<p>Lockheed said its share of the contract, which was awarded by the British Defense Ministry, was worth about $100 million over the 10 years.</p>
<p>The consortium will deliver voice, data and other wide-area networking services for the Royal Navy, Air Force and Army, it said.</p>
</text>
